            <ArticleTitle>Radiographic evaluation of the patient with chest pain of suspected myocardial origin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1451-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evaluation of the patient with suspected angina pectoris is discussed and an approach presented which makes use of radiologic tests in conjunction with exercise testing to quickly and efficiently determine the likelihood and severity of coronary artery disease. The relative merits and limitations of chest radiography, cardiac fluoroscopy, nuclear medicine, and coronary arteriography are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
